# .dockerignore
# Keeps the build context to what the images need: manifests, lockfile, sources,
# migrations and fixtures. A secret that never enters the context cannot end up
# in a layer, so .env is excluded here as well as in .gitignore.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.env
.env.*
*.log
test
**/test
docker-compose.yml
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
